ithub.io/post/2025-11-30-algograph/</link><pubDate>Sun, 30 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-30-algograph/</guid><description>AlgoGraph is an immutable graph library for Python with pipe-based transformers, declarative selectors, and lazy views.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-30-algograph/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Functional-Programming</media:title></media:content><category>Python</category><category>graphs</category><category>algorithms</category><category>functional-programming</category><category>data-structures</category><category>immutability</category></item><item><title>ZeroIPC: Shared Memory as a Computational Substrate</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-zeroipc/</link><pubDate>Mon, 06 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-zeroipc/</guid><description>ZeroIPC treats shared memory not as passive storage but as an active computational substrate, bringing futures, lazy evaluation, reactive streams, and CSP channels to IPC with zero-copy performance.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-zeroipc/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Functional-Programming</media:title></media:content><category>C++</category><category>Python</category><category>IPC</category><category>shared-memory</category><category>zero-copy</category><category>functional-programming</category><category>reactive-programming</category><category>codata</category><category>concurrency</category><category>lock-free</category><category>systems-programming</category></item><item><title>JAF: Streaming Boolean Algebra Over Nested JSON</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-12-jaf/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-12-jaf/</guid><description>A streaming data processing system implementing boolean algebra over nested JSON structures, with lazy evaluation, S-expression queries, and memory-efficient windowed operations.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-12-jaf/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Functional-Programming</media:title></media:content><category>Python</category><category>streaming</category><category>JSON</category><category>lazy-evaluation</category><category>functional-programming</category><category>boolean-algebra</category><category>data-processing</category><category>ETL</category></item><item><title>The Dot Ecosystem: From Simple Paths to Data Algebras</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-12-dotsuite/</link><pubDate>Sun, 15 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-12-dotsuite/</guid><description>A composable ecosystem of tools for manipulating nested data structures. From a simple helper function to a full data algebra, guided by purity, pedagogy, and the principle of least power.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-12-dotsuite/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Functional-Programming</media:title></media:content><category>Python</category><category>data-structures</category><category>JSON</category><category>functional-programming</category><category>API-design</category><category>category-theory</category><category>compositionality</category><category>Unix-philosophy</category></item><item><title>JSL: A Functional Language Where Code Is JSON</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-11-jsl/</link><pubDate>Wed, 20 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-11-jsl/</guid><description>A Lisp-like functi